W: 1 New ev&apos;ry morning is the love
W: our waking and uprising prove;
W: through sleep and darkness safely brought,
W: restored to life and pow&apos;r and thought.
W:
W: 2 New mercies, each returning day,
W: hover around us while we pray;
W: new perils past, new sins forgiv&apos;n,
W: new thoughts of God, new hopes of heav&apos;n.
W:
W: 3 If on our daily course our mind
W: be set to hallow all we find,
W: new treasures still of countless price,
W: God will provide for sacrifice.
W:
W: 4 Old friends, old scenes will lovelier be,
W: as more of heav&apos;n in each we see;
W: some sof&apos;ning gleam of love and prayer
W: shall dawn on ev&apos;ry cross and care.
W:
W: 5 The trivial round, the common task,
W: will furnish all we ought to ask:
W: room to deny ourselves, a road
W: to bring us daily nearer God.
W:
W: 6 Only, O Lord, in Thy dear love
W: fit us for perfect rest above;
W: and help us, this and ev&apos;ry day,
W: to live more nearly as we pray.</miscellaneous-field>
